      {
        "id": 226103,
        "name": "rickjonzz",
        "username": "rickjonzz",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rickjonzz/{size}/1934_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-25T14:44:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So far, the best I've done was get Oblivaeon down to 94 HP before the end of the Multiverse.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I had thought for a while&nbsp;that Effusion of Pain was the easiest shield to beat because it sometimes flipped itself out of the gate and on a couple of plays, it seemed pretty easy to beat - just keep the team together in Ob's Environment and wait for it. And since it's early game and I'm usually playing scrubs, l'd split the team and let him vaporize half of team, since they were going to get wiped anyway&nbsp;and now the shield was totally gone. But, then I spent most of my attempts this weekend just chasing him back and forth as he jumps between Environments leaving me more and more beat up. Or worse, I've got everyone in the right spot at the start of Ob's turn and he'd wipe out 1-2 heroes and then when the shield finally gets to go, it doesn't affect \"H\" heroes so it doesn't flip.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I honestly have been so bad at Oblivaeon Mode (I'm doing this on my ipad, but the game play is the same) that I started sorting the Scions from 1-3 and leaving Voss last because OMG he's such a pain late game.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If anyone's putting a guide together (and I'll happily help if I can), I'd love to see:</p>\n<p>1) Advice on the heroes and environments to use early in the game so you can flip shields faster.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2) Advice on the heroes and environments are good mid-game while you're collecting goodies and whittling down Oblivaeon.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>3) Advice on how to survive the end game when he's throwing all those \"wipe them out, all of them\" cards left and right.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:53.929Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
