        "id": 226105,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-27T04:04:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That data will be really interesting to see.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"FearLord\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5f8ce5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> FearLord:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As for the Scions, they have a difficulty ranking in the rule book between 1 - 3. Arguably Voss should be ranked higher than 3, as he’s pretty difficult to deal with early game and adds a whole extra wrinkle to the late game.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Faultless, Empyron and Sanction are the easiest 3 Scions. Faultless in particular can be a massive asset when flipped providing lots of healing and Power plays to the heroes, potentially for a while if you can keep him in play.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>At this point, I kind of wonder why they bothered with difficulty rankings on the Scions. I mean, it’s not like you don’t often see more than half of them in a single game. So they kind of all blur together into an overall average difficulty level, unless you start with easy ones and are extremely careful to manage them (and extremely lucky).</p>",
